<%# One membership delivery for the Ranked view.
    (See Session#broadcast_ranked_membership and ranked_queue_controller.js.)

    The Ranked view broadcasts on ONE stream, `sessions_ranked`, but every open
    page has its own filters. The server therefore cannot decide whether a row
    belongs on your screen — so it does not try. It ships this envelope: the
    session's filterable facts, plus the row already rendered for the section it
    would land in, and the page decides.

    The row travels inside a <template>. Its contents are inert and its ids are
    not in the document, so an envelope for a session the page filters out never
    puts a second `ranked_row_<id>` on the page, and one for a row already on
    screen never duplicates it. `ranked-queue#deliveryTargetConnected` reads the
    envelope, acts on it, and removes it.

    `draggable_row` follows the scheduling class, which is also the section the
    row is destined for — the client places it and the two agree.

    Locals:
      agent_session - the session %>
<div data-ranked-queue-target="delivery"
     hidden
     data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
     data-status="<%= agent_session.status %>"
     data-scheduling-class="<%= agent_session.priority_class %>"
     data-precedence="<%= agent_session.precedence %>">
  <template>
    <%= render "sessions/ranked_row",
          agent_session: agent_session,
          draggable_row: agent_session.priority_class == SessionGenesis::SPOT %>
  </template>
</div>
